{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2025-69204",
    "CVE-2025-68618",
    "CVE-2025-43965"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that ImageMagick incorrectly handled image depth values\nwhen processing MIFF image files. An attacker could use this issue to cause\na denial of service or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2025-43965)\n\nIt was discovered that ImageMagick incorrectly processed SVG images and\nMSL files. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2025-68618)\n\nIt was discovered that ImageMagick incorrectly handled memory when\nconverting MVG files. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2025-69204)",
  "id": "USN-8007-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in ImageMagick.",
